          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong poly-morphism
            is a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            with common
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi poly
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{poly}
            with the same
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{poly}(a,b) \coloneqq P(C(a,b))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            of the original hom-sets.
          %p
            These play a substantive rôle in
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinichi+Mochizuki"} Shinichi Mochizuki
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inter-universal+Teichm%C3%BCller+theory"} inter-universal Teichmüller theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Mochizuki12"}> Mochizuki 12, section 0
            ). Here we put these into the broader context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+enriching+categories"} change of enriching categories
            along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            as the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is a
            = succeed "-functor," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} equivariant
            version thereof.
          %h2#abstract_approach Abstract approach
          %p
            In the following, fix a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mi Cat
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C \in V Cat
                  \\,.
          %p
            Examples to keep in mind for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            are the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of sets considered as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
            for a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p Recall:
          #ChangeOfEnrichingCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+enriching+category"} change of enriching category
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                to itself)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon V\to V
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              to itself, the image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\ast(C)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              under the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+enriching+category"} change of enriching category
              is the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+objects"} hom objects
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_\ast(C)(a,b) \coloneqq F(C(a,b))
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              = succeed "-," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\ast(C)
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
              of those of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              suitably composed with the structure morphisms of the lax monoidal functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %p
            For the case of poly-morphisms the relevant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
            are
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
          #PowerSetFunctors.num_example
            %h6#examples Examples
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                  equipped with its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  an arbitrary
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi P
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Set
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \coloneqq P \;\colon\; Set \to Set
                  to be the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functor"} covariant
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
                  functor. This is lax monoidal since every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\subseteq T
                  gives a subset
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo ×
                          %mi V
                          %mo ⊆
                          %mi S
                          %mo ×
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\times V \subseteq S\times T
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  a group,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GSet"} GSet
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} category enriched in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi P
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi GSet
                        %mo →
                        %mi GSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \coloneqq P\;\colon\; GSet \to GSet
                  also be the covariant
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
                  functor, but for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  a
                  = succeed "-set," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S)
                  with the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi g
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi U
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi g
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        U\mapsto g\cdot U
                        \=
                        \\{g\cdot x \in S \mid x\in U\}
                        \\,.
          #PolyMorphisms.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (poly-morphisms)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a plain category and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \coloneqq P \colon Set \to Set
              the
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PowerSetFunctors"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^{poly}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    P_\ast(C)
            %p
              for the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+enriching+category"} change of enriching category
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChangeOfEnrichingCategory"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %p
              We say that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{poly}
              are the
              %strong poly-morphisms
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              Explicitly, this means
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              is defined to be
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^{poly}(a,b) \otimes C^{poly}(b,c) = P(C(a,b)) \otimes P(C(b,c)) \to P(C(a,b)\otimes B(b,c)) \to P(C(a,c)) = C^{poly}(a,c)
            %p
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
              map is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I \to P(I) \to P(C(a,a)) = C^{poly}(a,a)
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %strong poly-isomorphism
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is defined to be a poly-morphism of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi poly
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Core(C))^{poly}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+morphisms"} invertible morphisms
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %strong not
              in general the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi poly
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{poly}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi poly
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{poly}
              are actual isomorphisms in
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The above construction for enrichment in plain sets is considered (without the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            formulation) in:
          %ul
            %li#Mochizuki12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinichi+Mochizuki"}> Shinichi Mochizuki
              , section 0 of
              %em Inter-universal Teichmüller theory I, Construction of Hodge theaters
              (2012) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.kurims.kyoto-u.ac.jp/~motizuki/Inter-universal%20Teichmuller%20Theory%20I.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The construction for enrichment in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            is considered in
          %ul
            %li
              Alveen Chand,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"} Ittay Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em An ordered framework for partial multivalued functors
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.00746"} arXiv:1511.00746
        .revisedby
